Package: matebook-e-cameras
Architecture: amd64
Depends: matebook-e-cameras-dkms (= ${binary:Version}),
 v4l2loopback-dkms,
 python3 (>= 3.9),
 python3-gi,
 gir1.2-gstreamer-1.0,
 gstreamer1.0-plugins-base,
 gstreamer1.0-plugins-good,
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends}
Suggests: cheese, gstreamer1.0-tools, v4l-utils
Description: on-demand camera integration for Huawei MateBook E 2023
 Provides two ordinary V4L2 cameras backed by the Intel IPU6 controller,
 Hynix HI846 front sensor and Samsung S5K3L6 rear sensor on DRR-WXX.
 .
 Includes a private libcamera stack, automatic exposure and initial rear
 focus, a system bridge, and desktop enumeration rules. The sensors are
 released when applications close the cameras.

Package: matebook-e-cameras-dkms
Section: kernel
Architecture: all
Depends: dkms (>= 3.0.11), ${misc:Depends}
Description: DKMS camera drivers for Huawei MateBook E 2023
 Driver sources for the IPU bridge, Hynix HI846, Samsung S5K3L6 and
 DW9714 lens controller used by the MateBook E 2023 camera integration.
 .
 The ACPI and register integration is tested with the DRR-WXX tablet
 and Debian Linux 6.12.111. Matching kernel headers are needed for DKMS.
